WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.533 --> 00:00:09.074
It's not easy being a plant.

2
00:00:09.855 --> 00:00:13.598
Plants are often on the dinner menu for hungry animals and insects.

3
00:00:14.879 --> 00:00:16.340
Reproducing can be a challenge.

4
00:00:17.721 --> 00:00:20.924
Sometimes there aren't enough nutrients in the soil for plants to eat.

5
00:00:21.784 --> 00:00:23.766
So how have plants survived?

6
00:00:26.188 --> 00:00:26.928
They've adapted!

7
00:00:27.749 --> 00:00:31.272
Over millions of years, they've found unique ways to survive.

8
00:00:32.076 --> 00:00:35.718
Plants can't run from insects or other animals that are trying to eat them.

9
00:00:36.478 --> 00:00:38.519
But some plants can hide.

10
00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:42.221
They don't jump behind trees or scurry under rocks.

11
00:00:43.141 --> 00:00:46.023
Instead they use camouflage to hide from predators.

12
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:51.345
These plants have a natural shape or color that helps them blend in with their surroundings.

13
00:00:52.366 --> 00:00:57.228
The Lithops plant has an amazing way to hide itself—it looks like stones!

14
00:00:58.132 --> 00:01:01.915
These plants can be found in southern Africa where it is very dry.

15
00:01:02.695 --> 00:01:04.316
Lithops is a succulent.

16
00:01:05.217 --> 00:01:08.880
Succulents are plants with thick leaves that can store a lot of water.

17
00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.502
Cactuses and aloe plants are also succulents.

18
00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:16.805
Succulents usually live in deserts, where water is scarce.

19
00:01:17.546 --> 00:01:21.609
During the rainy season, Lithops' leaves push up from the soil.

20
00:01:22.369 --> 00:01:25.872
They soak up lots of water and become round like stones.

21
00:01:27.348 --> 00:01:32.770
Since the leaves look like rocks, animals leave them alone, letting them hide in plain sight!

22
00:01:33.531 --> 00:01:36.392
Lithops' leaves have a small slit on top.

23
00:01:37.192 --> 00:01:40.094
When blooms appear, they grow from the slit.

24
00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:44.155
It looks just like the blooms are growing between two stones.

25
00:01:45.156 --> 00:01:46.696
Some plants don't try to hide.

26
00:01:47.397 --> 00:01:51.218
The titan arum is too big to use camouflage to blend in.

27
00:01:52.059 --> 00:01:54.740
Its blooms are usually about two-and-a-half meters tall.

28
00:01:55.596 --> 00:01:58.618
That makes it one of the largest flowers in the world.

29
00:02:00.219 --> 00:02:04.842
This plant has a special adaptation to help it with reproduction: it stinks!

30
00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:10.566
The titan arum's enormous blossoms smell like dung or rotting flesh.

31
00:02:11.427 --> 00:02:15.089
This is really gross to humans, but it's not gross to flies.

32
00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:21.013
Titan arum plants live in Indonesia's warm, wet rainforests.

33
00:02:21.914 --> 00:02:24.996
When it blooms, the stems of the plant grow warm.

34
00:02:26.004 --> 00:02:28.586
That helps spread its smell far and wide.

35
00:02:29.587 --> 00:02:33.289
When flies smell the blossoms, they come and walk on the flowers.

36
00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.971
Bits of pollen stick to their legs.

37
00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:43.496
Then the flies travel to other titan arum flowers, spreading the pollen and helping the titan arum reproduce.

38
00:02:44.457 --> 00:02:50.761
Even though the plant blooms only once every few years, this stinky adaptation is key to the species'

39
00:02:50.821 --> 00:02:54.784
survival. Like humans, plants need to eat to survive.

40
00:02:55.764 --> 00:02:58.205
Most plants simply get their nutrients from soil.

41
00:02:59.126 --> 00:03:03.648
But soil in environments like swamps and marshes has few nutrients.

42
00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:08.271
So certain plants that live in these environments have become carnivores.

43
00:03:09.231 --> 00:03:11.072
That's right—they eat meat!

44
00:03:11.853 --> 00:03:16.315
Some carnivorous plants have sticky leaves that trap insects that land on them.

45
00:03:17.376 --> 00:03:18.937
Others have slippery leaves.

46
00:03:20.457 --> 00:03:24.780
Insects slide down the leaves into a pool of the plants' digestive juices.

47
00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:31.696
Usually carnivorous plants eat insects, but sometimes they eat small frogs or mammals.

48
00:03:32.857 --> 00:03:36.460
Venus flytraps are probably the most well-known carnivorous plants.

49
00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.503
They live in the swamps of the southeastern United States.

50
00:03:41.463 --> 00:03:44.265
They have pairs of leaves with small hairs on them.

51
00:03:45.286 --> 00:03:50.750
When an insect touches these hairs, the two leaves snap shut, trapping the insect inside.

52
00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.652
Then the plant digests the insect.

53
00:03:54.624 --> 00:03:57.645
This can take a flytrap a week or longer.

54
00:03:58.686 --> 00:04:01.267
But eventually it gets the nutrients it needs.

55
00:04:02.848 --> 00:04:07.870
Staying safe, reproducing, and getting enough nutrients can be challenging for plants.

56
00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.092
But plants are tough and have adapted to survive.

57
00:04:13.172 --> 00:04:17.534
The next time you see a plant, take a look and see how it has adapted to its

58
00:04:17.594 --> 00:04:21.836
environment. You might find something pretty cool—or weird!
